From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: thermal: add allwinner,sun60i-a733-ths

Enum entry only, and that is deliberate. The A733 needs two clocks, so it must
NOT join the sun20i-d1 / sun50i-a100 / sun50i-h6 / sun50i-h616 branch of the
first allOf, which caps clocks at one; the else branch with minItems: 2 is the
correct one and it applies by default. Staying out of the h616 branch also
leaves allwinner,sram forbidden, which is right -- that is an H616 erratum. And
staying out of the h3/d1 branch leaves #thermal-sensor-cells free to be 1, which
a five-sensor part needs.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thermal/allwinner,sun8i-a83t-ths.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thermal/allwinner,sun8i-a83t-ths.yaml
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
       - allwinner,sun50i-h5-ths
       - allwinner,sun50i-h6-ths
       - allwinner,sun50i-h616-ths
+      - allwinner,sun60i-a733-ths
 
   clocks:
     minItems: 1
